		(descr "Mantech K3599 1/4in (6.35mm) 3-conductor CLOSED (switched) open-frame phone jack, 6 solder lugs. MEASURED off the real part 2026-10-10 (recalibrated caliper): thin through-pin FLAT 1.33w x 0.5 thick (diag ~1.42, fits the 1.5 drill), along-row pitch 6.36mm c-c (3 legs/row), ROW SPACING 17.0mm c-c (MEASURED 2026-10-29 at the body exit without splay -- supersedes the earlier 16.55; legs FLEX across the rows so holes are forgiving). Fat legs TAPER to the thin through-pin and seat on the PCB (~6mm standoff, INFERRED -- confirm on a real mount). lug width 20.42mm, jack length 34.26mm, barrel axis 13.85mm below the board (MEASURED 2026-10-29, barrel centre to board plane -> JACK_Z 9.31; supersedes the inferred 13.9 and the stale 12.39). Barrel/bushing IN LINE with the legs at the +Y (back-wall) end; body extends -Y (forward, below the board). Pads 1/2/3 = Tip/Ring/Sleeve, CONFIRMED off the part 2026-10-10: TIP is furthest from the barrel opening (deepest, pad 1 at -Y); RING is the middle leg (pad 2); SLEEVE/GND is closest to the opening (pad 3 at +Y, the barrel end) -- matches the Conn_01x03 symbol pins 1/2/3. Barrel front = panel hole = +18.36 from the ring leg (12 from the sleeve leg, 7 from back-of-barrel to the tip leg). The 3 unnumbered pads are the switch/normalling lugs (soldered, no net in v1). BOTTOM-MOUNTED: place on B.Cu so the body hangs below the board.")
		(tags "jack TRS 6.35mm phone K3599 open-frame switched measured")
